menu "Passive CSI Config"

    config CSI_CHANNEL
        int "WiFi Channel to listen on"
        default 6
        help
            The 2.4 GHz channel your AP/hotspot is using.
            Run 'airport -I | grep channel' on macOS to find it.
            Valid range: 1-13.

    config CSI_CHANNEL_BW
        int "Channel bandwidth: 0=HT20 (20MHz)  1=HT40-above  2=HT40-below"
        default 1
        help
            Modern APs and phone hotspots almost always use HT40 (40MHz).
            HT40-above means the secondary channel is above the primary
            (e.g. primary=6, secondary=10).
            HT40-below means the secondary channel is below
            (e.g. primary=6, secondary=2).
            If you see zero data frames from your AP, try the other value.
            Default 1 (HT40-above) works for most iPhone hotspots on ch6.

    config CSI_LLTF_ONLY
        bool "Collect LLTF only (smaller CSI, higher throughput)"
        default y
        help
            LLTF (Legacy Long Training Field) is present in every frame.
            Enabling this limits CSI to 128 bytes (64 subcarriers) per frame
            and keeps the serial port from saturating.
            Disable only if you need HT-LTF data and have a fast baud rate.

endmenu
